

DischargeReady
From a 10-page clinical report to a clear care plan, double-checked by 
AI agents.
Naitik Srivastava  |  GL Bajaj Institute  of Technology and Management

The problem: discharge day confusion
~1 in 5
Medicare patients  are readmitted 
within 30 days (US CMS data)
Dense
10 pages of clinical shorthand,  ICD codes and abbreviations.
Complex
Multiple  drugs, different  times, hold rules and dose limits.
Easy to miss
Diet, activity limits and follow-up  dates buried in the text.

How DischargeReady works
1
Upload
Paste text or upload the 
discharge PDF.
2
Understand
Plain-language  summary in 
English, Hindi or Hinglish.
3
Act
Daily schedule, roadmap, 
checklist and calendar 
reminders.

Multi-agent architecture
1 · Medical Parser
Reads the report. Extracts 
diagnoses, meds, doses, 
restrictions, follow-ups.
2 · Care Plan & 
Timeline
Builds the daily schedule, 
roadmap and checklist in 
plain language.
3 · Patient Advocate / 
QA
Audits for missing, 
hallucinated or wrong-dose 
items.
Safety loop: issues found, plan sent back for a fix
Every checklist item carries a quote from the source report.

Features
Plain-language summary
Why you were admitted and what 
matters most.
Daily schedule + roadmap
Pill times, food rules and follow-ups 
in order.
Safety audit tab
Shows what the QA agent caught 
and fixed.
Hindi / Hinglish
Output in the patient’s own 
language.
Ask the report
Chat grounded only in the 
discharge text.
Read aloud + calendar
Voice playback and .ics reminders.

Why it matters
Safe by design
A second agent audits the first. 
Answers stay grounded in the 
report, with source quotes.
Accessible
Plain language, Hindi and 
Hinglish,  voice playback. Built for 
elderly patients  and caregivers.
Built to scale
Works on any discharge text. 
Ready for hospital and health-
record integration.
Decision support only. Not a replacement for medical advice.

